le has been modified.  Next is the main[7d editor window showing the file being edited.  The status line is the[8d third line from the bottom and shows important messages.  The bottom two[9d lines show the most commonly used shortcuts in the editor.[10d[K[11d Shortcuts are written as follows: Control-key sequences are notated with[12d a '^' and can be entered either by using the Ctrl key or pressing the Esc[13d key twice.  Meta-key sequences are notated with 'M-' and can be entered[14d using either the Alt, Cmd, or Esc key, depending on your keyboard setup.[15d Also, pressing Esc twice and then typing a three-digit decimal number[16d from 000 to 255 will enter the character with the corresponding value.[17d The following keystrokes are available in the main editor window.[18d Alternative keys are shown in parentheses:[19d[K[20d^G     (F1)      Display this help text[21d^X     (F2)      Close the current buffer / Exit from nano[2d[23;2H(B[0;7mG(B[m Help      (B[0;7m^O(B[m Write Out (B[0;7m^F(B[m Where Is  (B[0;7m^K(B[m Cut       (B[0;7m^T(B[m Execute   (B[0;7m^C(B[m Location[K[24;4HExit [15G(B[0;7mR(B[m Read File (B[0;7m^\(B[m Replace   (B[0;7m^U(B[m Paste     (B[0;7m^J(B[m Justify   (B[0;7m^/(B[m Go To[79G[1;3H(B[0;7mGNU nano 8.4[1;32H fixtures/sample.txt[1;71HModified(B[m[2dline 030 of the sample file[3dline 031 of the sample file[K[4dline 032 of the sample file[K[5dline 033 of the sample file[K[6dline 034 of the sample file[K[7dline 035 of the sample file[K[8dline 036 of the sample file[K[9dline 037 of the sample file[K[10dline 038 of the sample file[11dline 039 of the sample file[K[12dline 040 of the sample file[K[13dline 041 of the sample file[K[14dline 042 of the sample file[K[15dline 043 of the sample file[K[16dline 044 of the sample file[K[17dline 045 of the sample file[K[18dline 046 of the sample file[K[19dline 047 of the